{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > singleton_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']))\nq=dict(question='Does singleton ReadIndex preserve linearizable read safety after crash recovery when the durable log contains completed writes beyond a legally non-durable commit index, and a new leader answers before committing its current-term entry?',importance='A completed read can return a value older than a write completed before read invocation, violating the replicated state-machine read-safety contract even though no durable log entry is lost.',source_ids=[],participants=['Singleton raft member','Ready storage/application caller','Client register writes and read'],objects=['F-commit','Durable log','HardState.Commit','ReadState.Index','Applied register value'],contexts=['One voter, synchronous Ready/Advance interface','Crash preserves all MustSync flushes and loses later non-durable commit metadata','Application restores a real snapshot and replays committed entries in order with bounded batches'],event_paths=['Bootstrap and snapshot -> election -> batched durable writes A,B -> commit/apply B and respond -> crash -> restore durable state -> replay -> election -> ReadIndex before current-term commitment -> apply strictly beyond returned read index -> return register value'],activity_classes=['A1','A2','A3','A5','A6','A7'],behavior_ids=['B-read','B-recovery','B-replication'],fact_ids=['F-commit'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-storage':'MustSync producer and caller durability boundary determine what survives crash.','B-application':'Returned committed batches establish actual applied state before read service.','B-election':'Actual self-vote persistence and new-leader no-op create the restart authority context.','B-client':'Linearizable read interface and caller-owned storage/application duties.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Non-singleton reads wait for current-term commitment.','ReadIndex requests may be lost and retried, but this question concerns an actual completed result rather than missing completion.','Finishing all replay before serving any read would mask the stale fence; the interface instead permits service once application is beyond the returned index.','After remaining replay the register reaches B again; that does not repair the earlier completed response.'],unknowns=[],disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',priority=3,trigger_rationale='Singleton branch precedes the current-term commit gate; MustSync excludes commit-only changes. Actual exploration reconstructed a legal durable prefix and returned A after B had completed, while satisfying even strict applied > read index. A fresh fixed safety comparison must validate this history rather than treating the exploration as Evidence.')\nfor o in m['facts']+m['behaviors']:\n if o['id'] in q['fact_ids']+q['behavior_ids']+list(q['supporting_behavior_ids']):q['source_ids']+=o['source_ids']\nq['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(q['source_ids']+['s-read-client-contract','s-read-ready-contract','s-read-api','s-mustsync-contract','s-mustsync-producer','s-snapshot-create']))\nclaim='O-singleton-read-safety';ss=['s-read-client-contract','s-read-ready-contract','s-read-api','s-mustsync-contract','s-mustsync-producer','s-propose','s-init','s-logappend','s-applyable']\np=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Fix the read-safety responsibility from the interface under an explicitly permitted durability model, independently of request-loss progress semantics.',question=q,obligation=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='A completed linearizable read served using a returned ReadState after applying strictly beyond its index must reflect the latest completed preceding register write when no later write intervenes, including after recovery from loss of only non-durable metadata.',source_ids=ss,scope=dict(description='Singleton register state machine using ReadOnlySafe, legal Ready processing and a crash preserving all synchronized state; recovered application follows committed-entry order and serves a read only after satisfying the returned index.',assumptions=['Write completion follows commitment and actual application.','Read invocation occurs after that write completion and after restart; no concurrent or intervening writes.','All MustSync=true work flushes preceding staged writes and log entries; only later MustSync=false metadata may be lost.','Snapshot is created from actually applied state and configuration.'],excluded=['No Byzantine storage, lost synchronized log entries or reused request context.','No requirement that every ReadIndex request completes.','No claim about multi-voter behavior.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=ss,expectation_ids=['s-read-client-contract','s-read-ready-contract','s-read-api','s-mustsync-contract'],derivation='Ready.ReadStates and RawNode.ReadIndex explicitly authorize linearizable local reads once applied is beyond the returned index. For a register with completed B preceding read invocation and no later writes, linearizability requires B. Ready.MustSync explicitly permits non-durable writes when false, and the producer does not sync commit-only HardState changes. Crash recovery from a durable log ahead of the last synchronized commit therefore belongs to the interface scope. Request-loss permission cannot authorize an incorrect completed read.',applicability='Application and persistence contracts are met in the same crash/restart history; the predicate compares actual read output to a prior completed register write using independent operation identity.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Delaying reads until all committed replay completes is a stronger caller policy than the returned-index condition; the fixed driver uses the documented index condition conservatively.'])),bindings=[dict(id='bind-singleton-read',material_id='s-propose',symbol='stepLeader',start_line=1345,end_line=1367,description='Singleton read response bypasses the ordinary current-term commitment check.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['s-read-ready-contract','s-read-api'],rationale='This branch chooses the read index later consumed under the linearizable-read interface.')]),dict(id='bind-mustsync',material_id='s-mustsync-producer',symbol='MustSync',start_line=193,end_line=200,description='Durability flag allows commit-only metadata to remain non-durable.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['s-mustsync-contract'],rationale='Determines the legal recovered commit/log relationship for this responsibility.')])],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['0fd1590766834982ba62b47eac531581','B-read','B-recovery','s-mustsync-contract','s-read-ready-contract'],answered='Exploration 0fd1590766834982ba62b47eac531581 completed both commands at indexes 3 and 4 with value B, durable last=4 and durable commit=2. Restart from that actual durable state elected term 3, returned ReadState index 2, then served A after applying index 3 (>2). Remaining replay restored B at index 4. This establishes construction knowledge and an actual endpoint in exploration, not formal Evidence.',remaining=['Fresh fixed execution and correspondence review are needed for the safety obligation.','The independent delayed-configuration read-continuation contract remains unresolved.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The decisive distinction is an incorrect completed result, not a dropped request or finite timeout.'))\njson.dump(p,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 singleton_obligation.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));x=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(x.stdout,x.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
